0824                         
0825                         ; The depletion of energy from the space ship’s main storage bank 
0826                         ; and its shields is an important function in this program. The following
0827                         ; group of subroutines is called to delete the energy from the ship, 
0828                         ; and to check the energy level of the ship. The subroutine labeled 
0829                         ; ELOS deletes the amount of energy contained in the index register 
0830                         ; from the ship’s protective shields. The least significant half of the 
0831                         ; energy to be deleted must be stored in the most significant half of 
0832                         ; the index register, and the most significant half of the energy must 
0833                         ; be stored in the least significant half of the index register. By switching
0834                         ; the two eight bit values around in this manner, the STX instruction
0835                         ; will store the energy in the desired order in memory (the least 
0836                         ; significant half in the lower address of the pair of memory locations). 
0837                         ; The amount of energy deleted is first output to the display device to 
0838                         ; inform the operator of the loss. The shield energy level is checked, 
0839                         ; and if sufficient, the energy is removed from the shield. If the level 
0840                         ; is not high enough to absorb the loss, the remaining shield energy is 
0841                         ; transferred to the main supply, and the loss is taken from the main 
0842                         ; storage bank. If at this time the main supply is not enough, the ship 
0843                         ; is out of energy, and the game is over. Otherwise, since the shield 
0844                         ; energy is zero, the warning message is output and an additional 25 
0845                         ; percent of the energy loss is depleted from the main supply as a 
0846                         ; penalty. The listing of ELOS and its supporting subroutines is shown 
0847                         ; next. 
0848                         
0849 0798 df 2a              ELOS        STX         STORE3      ; Save energy value 
0850 079a ce 00 2a                       LDX         #STORE3     ; Set pointer to value to be converted
0851 079d c6 02                          LDAB        #$02        ; Double precision conversion
0852 079f bd 05 29                       JSR         BINDEC      ; Convert to BCD for message
0853 07a2 ce 03 13                       LDX         #Msg19a+3   ; Set pntr to least signif digit of energy 
0854 07a5 c6 04                          LDAB        #$04        ; Set digit counter
0855 07a7 bd 06 62                       JSR         DIGPRT      ; Put digit in message
0856 07aa ce 02 ff                       LDX         #MSG19      ; Set pointer to energy loss message
0857 07ad 8d e6                          BSR         LR6         ; Print energy loss message
0858 07af de 2a                          LDX         STORE3      ; Restore value for routines
0859 07b1 df 26                          STX         STORE1      ; To follow
0860                         
0861 07b3 8d 23              ELS1        BSR         CKSD        ; Is shield energy sufficient?
0862 07b5 24 32                          BCC         FMSD        ; Yes, delete from shields and return 
0863                         
0864 07b7 de 44              SDO1        LDX         DVSE        ; Move shield energy to main storage
0865 07b9 df 26                          STX         STORE1      ; Remove energy from shields
0866 07bb 8d 2c                          BSR         FMSD        ; Fetch energy to be deleted
0867 07bd 8d 41                          BSR         TOMN        ; Move shield energy to main storage
0868 07bf de 2a                          LDX         STORE3      ; 
0869 07c1 df 26                          STX         STORE1      ; Store for routines
0870                         
0871 07c3 8d 17              SDO         BSR         CKMN        ; Energy enough?
0872 07c5 25 53                          BCS         EOUT1       ; No, ship out of energy
0873 07c7 8d 24                          BSR         FMMN        ; Yes, take from main
0874 07c9 ce 03 15                       LDX         #MSG20      ; Print WARNING!
0875 07cc 8d c7                          BSR         LR6         ; DANGER - SHIELD ENERGY 000
0876 07ce c6 02                          LDAB        #$02        ; Divide energy loss by 2 twice
0877 07d0 8d 3d                          BSR         DVD         ; To divide by 4
0878 07d2 8d 08                          BSR         CKMN        ; Enough main energy for penalty?
0879 07d4 25 44                          BCS         EOUT1       ; No, out of energy message
0880 07d6 20 15                          BRA         FMMN        ; Yes, take penalty and return
0881                         
0882 07d8 de 68              CKSD        LDX         PDVSE       ; Check shield energy level
0883 07da 20 02                          BRA         CK1         ; Against requested level
0884                         
0885 07dc de 66              CKMN        LDX         PDVME       ; Check main energy level 
0886                         
0887 07de a6 01              CK1         LDAA        $01,X       ; Fetch most significant half
0888 07e0 91 27                          CMPA        STORE1+$1   ; Is most significant half =0?
0889 07e2 26 35                          BNE         ELOS1       ; No, return with flags set up
0890 07e4 a6 00              CK2         LDAA        0,X         ; If > =, return with C flag set
0891 07e6 91 26                          CMPA        STORE1      ; If less than, C flag reset
0892 07e8 39                             RTS                     ; Return
0893                         
0894 07e9 de 68              FMSD        LDX         PDVSE       ; Set pointer to shield energy
0895 07eb 20 02                          BRA         FM1         ; Subtract energy from shields
0896                         
0897 07ed de 66              FMMN        LDX         PDVME       ; Set pointer to main storage 
0898                         
0899 07ef a6 00              FM1         LDAA        0,X         ; Fetch least significant half of energy
0900 07f1 90 26                          SUBA        STORE1      ; Subtract least significant half of loss
0901 07f3 a7 00                          STAA        0,X         ; Return to storage
0902 07f5 a6 01                          LDAA        $01,X       ; Fetch most significant half of energy
0903 07f7 92 27                          SBCA        STORE1+$1   ; Subtract most significant half of loss 
0904 07f9 a7 01                          STAA        $01,X       ; Return to storage
0905 07fb 39                             RTS                     ;  
0906                          
0907 07fc de 68              TOSD        LDX         PDVSE       ; Set pointer to shield energy
0908 07fe 20 02                          BRA         TO1         ; Add energy to shields
0909                         
0910 0800 de 66              TOMN        LDX         PDVME       ; Set pointer to main energy 
0911 0802 a6 00              TO1         LDAA        0,X         ; Fetch least significant half of energy 
0912 0804 9b 26                          ADDA        STORE1      ; Add least significant half of loss
0913 0806 a7 00                          STAA        0,X         ; Return to storage
0914 0808 a6 01                          LDAA        $01,X       ; Fetch most significant half of energy 
0915 080a 99 27                          ADCA        STORE1+$1   ; Add most significant half of loss
0916 080c a7 01                          STAA        $01,X       ; Return to storage
0917 080e 39                             RTS                     ; 
0918                         
0919 080f 5d                 DVD         TSTB                    ; Divide the double
0920 0810 76 00 27                       ROR         STORE1+$1   ;  precision value
0921 0813 76 00 26                       ROR         STORE1      ;   by two the number
0922 0816 5a                             DECB                    ;    of times indicated in B
0923 0817 26 f6                          BNE         DVD         ; 
0924 0819 39                 ELOS1       RTS                     ; Return
0925 081a 7e 06 5d           EOUT1       JMP         EOUT        ; 
0926                         
0927                         
0928                         ; The removal of energy from the main supply for the execution of 
0929                         ; commands, firing phasors and torpedoes, and moving through the 
0930                         ; galaxy is provided by the ELOM subroutine. The amount of energy 
0931                         ; to be removed is stored in the index register (as described in the 
0932                         ; ELOS subroutine) when the ELOM subroutine is called. If the main 
0933                         ; energy bank contains enough energy, the energy is deleted, and the 
0934                         ; subroutine returns to the calling program. If there is not enough 
0935                         ; energy, the shield energy is transferred to the main storage bank in 
0936                         ; an effort to provide for the loss. If this does not provide sufficient 
0937                         ; energy, the game is over. However, if the transfer does produce the 
0938                         ; energy needed in the main supply, the energy will be removed; and 
0939                         ; since the shield energy has been reduced to zero, an additional 25 
0940                         ; percent of the energy loss will be deleted from the main supply as a 
0941                         ; penalty.
0942                         
0943 081d 8d bd              ELOM        BSR         CKMN        ; Enough energy in main?
0944 081f 24 cc                          BCC         FMMN        ; Yes, take from main and return
0945 0821 de 26                          LDX         STORE1      ; No, save value of energy loss
0946 0823 df 2a                          STX         STORE3      ; Transfer shield energy and try again
0947 0825 7e 07 b7                       JMP         SDO1        ; 
0948                         
0949                         
0950                         ; The amount of energy transferred to or from the shields and the 
0951                         ; energy to be fired by the phasor is entered by the operator. The EIN 
0952                         ; subroutine is called to input these energy values. The first entry is 
0953                         ; checked to determine whether it is a minus sign, used in the shield 
0954                         ; entry. Location 55 on page 00 will be all zeros if the value is to be 
0955                         ; positive, and non-zero for a negative entry. Each digit entered is 
0956                         ; checked for validity, and then the ASCII code is masked off, resulting
0957                         ; in the BCD digits being stored in locations 54 through 51. The 
0958                         ; units digit is stored in location 51. Four digits must be entered by 
0959                         ; the operator when this routine is called. If the input is found to be 
0960                         ; invalid, the routine returns with the N flag set to T.’ If the input is 
0961                         ; valid, the N flag is reset upon returning to the calling program. 
0962                         
0963 0828 de 74              EIN         LDX         PDG5TH      ; Set pointer to start of digit store
0964 082a 6f 00                          CLR         0,X         ; Clear sign indicator 
0965 082c bd 0f 80                       JSR         INPUT       ; Get first character 
0966 082f 81 2d                          CMPA        #'-         ; Negative sign?  (was $AD)
0967 0831 26 05                          BNE         EN2         ; No, check digit 
0968 0833 a7 00                          STAA        0,X         ; Make negative indicator not =0 
0969 0835 bd 0f 80           EN1         JSR         INPUT       ; Get next character 
0970 0838 09                 EN2         DEX                     ; Advance storage pointer 
0971 0839 a7 00                          STAA        0,X         ; Store digit 
0972 083b bd 05 bd                       JSR         FNUM        ; Valid digit? 
0973 083e 2b 0a                          BMI         EIN1        ; No, return with N flag set 
0974 0840 a6 00                          LDAA        0,X         ; Yes, fetch digit 
0975 0842 84 0f                          ANDA        #$0F        ; Mask off ASCII bits 
0976 0844 a7 00                          STAA        0,X         ; Save BCD value 
0977 0846 9c 72                          CPX         PDG1ST      ; End of input? 
0978 0848 26 eb                          BNE         EN1         ; No, fetch next digit 
0979 084a 39                 EIN1        RTS                     ; Yes, return 
0980                         
0981                         
0982                         ; When the space ship destroys an alien ship or space station, the 
0983                         ; result is the elimination of the alien ship or space station from the 
0984                         ; galaxy. The subroutine DLET is called to perform this function. 
0985                         ; First, the sector location of the object is cleared by storing a CO in 
0986                         ; the data table at the location indicated by the index register. From 
0987                         ; this location, the identity of the object to be deleted is ascertained. 
0988                         ; A pointer is then formed indicating the location of the quadrant in 
0989                         ; the galaxy content table from which the object is to be removed. If 
0990                         ; the object was a space station, it is removed from the galaxy and the 
0991                         ; number of space stations is decremented. If this value goes to zero, a 
0992                         ; warning message is output to inform the operator that the last space 
0993                         ; station has been destroyed. If an alien ship is destroyed, it is removed 
0994                         ; from the galaxy and its count is decremented. When the number of 
0995                         ; alien ships reaches zero, the game is over and the operator has successfully
0996                         ; completed the mission.
0997                         
0998 084b 86 c0              DLET        LDAA        #$C0        ; Load with clear character 
0999 084d a7 00                          STAA        0,X         ; Clear object from table
1000 084f df 22                          STX         PNTR2       ; Save table location
1001 0851 96 4c                          LDAA        CQLSS       ; Get quadrant location
1002 0853 8b c0                          ADDA        #$C0        ; Form galaxy table pointer
1003 0855 bd 09 51                       JSR         ATINX1      ; Place pointer in index
1004 0858 df 24                          STX         PNTR3       ; Set table pointer
1005 085a de 22                          LDX         PNTR2       ; Fetch table location
1006 085c bd 09 59                       JSR         COMPAR      ; Space station hit? 
1007 085f 26 15                          BNE         DLAS        ; No, delete alien ship 
1008 0861 de 24                          LDX         PNTR3       ; Fetch galaxy pointer
1009 0863 a6 00                          LDAA        0,X         ; Get quadrant contents
1010 0865 84 37                          ANDA        #$37        ; Delete space station
1011 0867 a7 00                          STAA        0,X         ; Restore quadrant in galaxy 
1012 0869 97 35                          STAA        CQC         ; Place new contents
1013 086b 7a 00 4e                       DEC         NSS         ; Decrement number of space stations
1014 086e 26 1b                          BNE         DLET1       ; If more left, return
1015 0870 ce 04 db                       LDX         #MSG37      ; If number of space stations =0,
1016 0873 7e 05 06                       JMP         MSG         ;  print warning message & return
1017                         
1018 0876 de 24              DLAS        LDX         PNTR3       ; Fetch galaxy pointer 
1019 0878 a6 00                          LDAA        0,X         ; Get quadrant contents
1020 087a 80 10                          SUBA        #$10        ; Delete 1 alien ship from quadrant
1021 087c a7 00                          STAA        0,X         ; Restore to galaxy
1022 087e 97 35                          STAA        CQC         ; Save new contents
1023 0880 7a 00 4f                       DEC         NAS         ; Decrement number of alien ships 
1024 0883 26 06                          BNE         DLET1       ; More aliens, return
1025 0885 ce 03 d4                       LDX         #MSG27      ; All aliens destroyed!
1026 0888 7e 06 4d                       JMP         DONE        ; Print CONGRATULATIONS,
1027 088b 39                 DLET1       RTS                     ; Start new game
1028                         
1029                         
1030                         ; The final group of subroutines to be presented deals with the 
1031                         ; movement of the space ship through the galaxy, and the tracking of 
1032                         ; the torpedo within the quadrant. Moving an object through the 
1033                         ; galaxy is performed with the use of a table referred to as the 
1034                         ; COURSE TABLE. The course table, presented next, is located at the 
1035                         ; beginning of page 00, and contains 16 pairs of row and column dis¬ 
1036                         ; placement values. There is one pair of displacement values for each 
1037                         ; possible direction of movement. The first value of each pair is the 
1038                         ; column displacement; the second value is the row displacement. 
1039                         ; The entries in the course table are made up of the binary values 2, 1, 
1040                         ; 0, -1, and -2. A displacement of 1 advances the object one half of a 
1041                         ; sector for each sector move made. So, for example, if the course was 
1042                         ; chosen as 8.5, the displacement value for the column is two, and for 
1043                         ; the row is one. This means that for every column moved to the right, 
1044                         ; the object would move one half of a row down. A move is made by 
1045                         ; the program by separating the row and column location of the object 
1046                         ; to be moved, rotating each to the left once, and using the adjusted 
1047                         ; values to calculate the move. Then, for each sector move made, the 
1048                         ; row and column displacement is added to the adjusted row and 
1049                         ; column location. When the move is completed, the adjusted values 
1050                         ; are rotated to the right once, and then combined to give a new sector 
1051                         ; location to the object. By using this method it is possible for the 
1052                         ; direction of travel to be broken down to every 22 l A degrees. 
1053                         
1054                         ;---
1055                         
1056                         ; The subroutine DRCT is called to input the course direction from 
1057                         ; the operator through the input device. The two digits defining the 
1058                         ; move are checked for validity when entered, and then used to form a 
1059                         ; pointer to the course table. If the input is valid, the routine returns 
1060                         ; with the Z flag reset, and the pointer stored in location 20 on page 
1061                         ; 00. If invalid, the Z flag is set before returning. The ACTV subroutine
1062                         ; is then called to fetch the displacement values from the course 
1063                         ; table, and store the column displacement in location 2D and the row 
1064                         ; displacement in location 2C. It then sets up the adjusted row and 
1065                         ; column values, and stores them in locations 2E and 2F respectively. 
1066                         ;
1067                         ; The subroutine labeled TRK is called to make the individual sector
1068                         ; moves. First, the quadrant crossing flag is cleared. The column 
1069                         ; displacement is then added to the adjusted column location, and a 
1070                         ; quadrant crossing to the left or right is checked. If the crossing did 
1071                         ; occur, the crossing flag is set, and the adjusted column is corrected to 
1072                         ; indicate the new column value. The crossing is then checked for a 
1073                         ; move out of the galaxy, which would be indicated by the TRK subroutine
1074                         ; returning with the Z flag set. If the move is not out of the 
1075                         ; galaxy, the new quadrant location is stored at location 4C on page 
1076                         ; 00. The row displacement is then added to the adjusted row location, 
1077                         ; and a quadrant crossing up and down is checked. If a quadrant is 
1078                         ; crossed, the crossing flag is set and a move out of the galaxy is 
1079                         ; checked. If the crossing is out of the galaxy, the routine returns with 
1080                         ; the Z flag set. Otherwise, the new quadrant location is stored at location
1081                         ; 4C, and the routine returns with the Z flag reset. The final subroutine
1082                         ; of this group is called RWCM, and is called to restore the adjusted row
1083                         ; and column locations to the single byte used to define the 
1084                         ; final location of the object moved.
1085                         
1086                                     
1087 088c bd 0f 80           DRCT        JSR         INPUT       ; Input first course number 
1088 088f 81 31                          CMPA        #$31        ; Is input less than 1? (was $B1)
1089                         ;x        x BCS         ZRET        ; ***************replaced...        
1090 0891 2d 25                          BLT         ZRET        ; Yes, illegal input 
1091 0893 81 39                          CMPA        #$39        ; Is input greater than 8? (was $B9)
1092                         ;x        x BCC         ZRET        ; *************** replaced...
1093 0895 2c 21                          BGE         ZRET        ; Yes, illegal input 
1094 0897 84 0f                          ANDA        #$0F        ; No, mask off ASCII bits 
1095 0899 48                             ASLA                    ; If good times 2 
1096 089a 16                             TAB                     ; And save in B
1097 089b 86 2e                          LDAA        #'.         ; (was $AE)
1098 089d bd 0f 89                       JSR         PRINT       ; Print decimal point 
1099 08a0 bd 0f 80                       JSR         INPUT       ; Input second course number 
1100 08a3 81 30                          CMPA        #'0         ; Is digit zero? (was $B0)
1101 08a5 27 04                          BEQ         CR1         ; Yes, continue process 
1102 08a7 81 35                          CMPA        #'5         ; No, is digit =5? (was $B5)
1103 08a9 26 0d                          BNE         ZRET        ; No, return with Z flag set 
1104 08ab 84 01              CR1         ANDA        #$01        ; Mask off all but first bit 
1105 08ad 1b                             ABA                     ; Add first number input 
1106 08ae 48                             ASLA                    ; 
1107 08af 80 04                          SUBA        #$04        ; And form pointer to course table 
1108 08b1 97 21                          STAA        PNTR1+$1    ; Save pointer in temporary storage
1109 08b3 4f                             CLRA                    ;  
1110 08b4 97 20                          STAA        PNTR1       ; Clear least significant byte of pointer
1111 08b6 4c                             INCA                    ; Reset Z flag 
1112 08b7 39                             RTS                     ; Before returning 
1113 08b8 4f                 ZRET        CLRA                    ; Set Z flag 
1114 08b9 39                             RTS                     ; And return 
1115                         
1116 08ba 9f 22              ACTV        STS         PNTR2       ; Save stack pointer temporarily 
1117 08bc 9e 58                          LDS         PSTR51      ; Set stack to storage area 
1118 08be 96 36                          LDAA        SLOSS       ; Get present location 
1119 08c0 16                             TAB                     ; Save temporarily 
1120 08c1 c4 07                          ANDB        #$07        ; Mask out column 
1121 08c3 58                             ASLB                    ; Multiply by 2 
1122 08c4 37                             PSHB                    ; Store adjusted column 
1123 08c5 84 38                          ANDA        #$38        ; Mask out row 
1124 08c7 44                             LSRA                    ; 
1125 08c8 44                             LSRA                    ; Set up times 2 value 
1126 08c9 36                             PSHA                    ; Save adjusted row 
1127 08ca de 20                          LDX         PNTR1       ; Get displacement table pointer 
1128 08cc a6 00                          LDAA        0,X         ; Get column movement 
1129 08ce 36                             PSHA                    ; Store column displacement < 
1130 08cf a6 01                          LDAA        $01,X       ; Get row movement 
1131 08d1 36                             PSHA                    ; Store row displacement 
1132 08d2 9e 22                          LDS         PNTR2       ; Restore stack pointer
1133 08d4 39                             RTS                     ; 
1134                         
1135 08d5 7f 00 32           TRK         CLR         CF          ; Clear quadrant crossing flag 
1136 08d8 96 2f                          LDAA        STORE5+$1   ; Get adjusted column 
1137 08da 9b 2d                          ADDA        STORE4+$1   ; Add column move 
1138 08dc 97 2f                          STAA        STORE5+$1   ; Save temporarily current column 
1139 08de 2a 12                          BPL         NOBK        ; If no left crossing, branch 
1140 08e0 84 0f                          ANDA        #$0F        ; Left crossing correction 
1141 08e2 97 2f                          STAA        STORE5+$1   ; And save new adjusted column 
1142 08e4 7c 00 32                       INC         CF          ; Indicate left crossing 
1143 08e7 96 4c                          LDAA        CQLSS       ; And decrement current column 
1144 08e9 84 07                          ANDA        #$07        ; Is CQC =0? 
1145 08eb 27 56                          BEQ         TRK1        ; Yes, return with Z set 
1146 08ed 7a 00 4c                       DEC         CQLSS       ; No, decrement CQC 
1147 08f0 20 17                          BRA         RMV         ; Do row move 
1148                         
1149 08f2 81 10              NOBK        CMPA        #$10        ; Quadrant crossing right 
1150 08f4 25 13                          BCS         RMV         ; No, do row move 
1151 08f6 84 0f                          ANDA        #$0F        ; Yes, correct and 
1152 08f8 97 2f                          STAA        STORE5+$1   ; Save new adjusted column 
1153 08fa 7c 00 32                       INC         CF          ; Indicate crossing by making 
1154                         ;                                   ; Crossing flag non-zero 
1155 08fd 96 4c                          LDAA        CQLSS       ; Fetch current quadrant location 
1156 08ff 84 07                          ANDA        #$07        ; Separate column entry 
1157 0901 4c                             INCA                    ; Increment column entry 
1158 0902 81 08                          CMPA        #$08        ; Move out of galaxy 
1159 0904 27 3d                          BEQ         TRK1        ; Yes, return with flags set 
1160 0906 7c 00 4c                       INC         CQLSS       ; No, increment quadrant column 
1161                         
1162 0909 96 2e              RMV         LDAA        STORE5      ; Get adjusted row value 
1163 090b 9b 2c                          ADDA        STORE4      ; Add movement 
1164 090d 97 2e                          STAA        STORE5      ; Save new adjusted row 
1165 090f 2a 14                          BPL         NOUP        ; If not up, jump 
1166 0911 84 0f                          ANDA        #$0F        ; Move up one quadrant, correct 
1167 0913 97 2e                          STAA        STORE5      ; And save new adjusted value 
1168 0915 7c 00 32                       INC         CF          ; Make crossing flag non-zero 
1169 0918 96 4c                          LDAA        CQLSS       ; Decrement quadrant row 
1170 091a 16                             TAB                     ; Save temporarily 
1171 091b 84 38                          ANDA        #$38        ; Is quadrant row =0? 
1172 091d 27 24                          BEQ         TRK1        ; Yes, return with Z flag set 
1173 091f c0 08                          SUBB        #$08        ; No, decrement current quadrant row 
1174 0921 d7 4c                          STAB        CQLSS       ; Save new current quadrant 
1175 0923 20 1a                          BRA         CKX         ; Then perform crossing logic 
1176                         
1177                         
1178 0925 81 10              NOUP        CMPA        #$10        ; Quadrant crossing down? 
1179 0927 25 16                          BCS         CKX         ; No, check for crossing flag 
1180 0929 84 0f                          ANDA        #$0F        ; Yes, correct and 
1181 092b 97 2e                          STAA        STORE5      ; Save new adjusted row 
1182 092d 7c 00 32                       INC         CF          ; Indicate crossing 
1183 0930 96 4c                          LDAA        CQLSS       ; Then increment quadrant row
1184 0932 16                             TAB                     ; Save temporarily
1185 0933 84 38                          ANDA        #$38        ; Separate row entry
1186 0935 8b 08                          ADDA        #$08        ; Increment row value 
1187 0937 81 40                          CMPA        #$40        ; Out of galaxy?
1188 0939 27 08                          BEQ         TRK1        ; Yes, return with Z flag set
1189 093b cb 08                          ADDB        #$08        ; No, increment row
1190 093d d7 4c                          STAB        CQLSS       ; Save new current quadrant
1191                         
1192 093f 26 02              CKX         BNE         TRK1        ; Return with Z flag reset
1193 0941 86 01                          LDAA        #$01        ; If not, reset it
1194 0943 39                 TRK1        RTS                     ; 
1195                         
1196 0944 96 2f              RWCM        LDAA        STORE5+$1   ; Fetch adjusted column 
1197 0946 44                             LSRA                    ; Adjust position
