1459                         
1460                         ; The commands, input by the operator to direct the operation of 
1461                         ; the space ship, are controlled by the COMMAND INPUT routine, 
1462                         ; labeled CMND. This routine (which immediately follows the short 
1463                         ; range scan) begins by deleting ten units of energy from the main 
1464                         ; storage bank to simulate the loss of energy resulting from the operation
1465                         ; of the ship’s control panel. The second byte of the random number
1466                         ; storage is then decremented to increase the random number 
1467                         ; generator’s overall randomness. The command request message is 
1468                         ; then output to the display device, followed by a call to the input 
1469                         ; routine to receive the command from the input device. If the character
1470                         ; input matches one of the ASCII codes (indicating a valid command),
1471                         ; the proper routine is entered to perform the command. If the 
1472                         ; character is not a valid command entry, the program simply requests 
1473                         ; the command input again.
1474                         
1475 0b39 ce 0a 00           CMND        LDX         #$0A00      ; Delete ten units of energy 
1476 0b3c df 26                          STX         STORE1      ; For each command
1477 0b3e bd 08 1d                       JSR         ELOM        ;
1478 0b41 7a 00 34                       DEC         RNM+$1      ; Randomize random number 
1479                         
1480 0b44 ce 02 15           CMD         LDX         #MSG12      ; Set pointer to command message 
1481 0b47 bd 05 06                       JSR         MSG         ; Request command input 
1482 0b4a bd 0f 80                       JSR         INPUT       ; Input command 
1483                         
1484 0b4d 81 30                          CMPA        #'0         ; Ship movement? ( was $B0 )
1485 0b4f 26 03                          BNE         NCRSE       ; No, try next
1486 0b51 7e 0c 4c                       JMP         CRSE        ; Yes, input course
1487 0b54 81 31              NCRSE       CMPA        #'1         ; Short range scan? ( was $B1 )
1488 0b56 26 03                          BNE         NSRSCN      ; No, try next
1489 0b58 7e 0a 65                       JMP         SRSCN       ; Yes, display quadrant 
1490 0b5b 81 32              NSRSCN      CMPA        #'2         ; Long range scan? ( was $B2 )
1491 0b5d 26 03                          BNE         NLRSCN      ; No, try next 
1492 0b5f 7e 0b 7e                       JMP         LRSCN       ; Yes, print long range scan 
1493 0b62 81 33              NLRSCN      CMPA        #'3         ; Galaxy printout?( was $B3 )
1494 0b64 26 03                          BNE         NGXPRT      ; No, try next 
1495 0b66 7e 0b d3                       JMP         GXPRT       ; Yes, print galaxy
1496 0b69 81 34              NGXPRT      CMPA        #'4         ; Shield energy? ( was $B4 )
1497 0b6b 26 03                          BNE         NSHEN       ; No, try next
1498 0b6d 7e 0c 13                       JMP         SHEN        ; Yes, adjust shields
1499 0b70 81 35              NSHEN       CMPA        #'5         ; Phasor control? ( was $B5 )
1500 0b72 26 03                          BNE         NPHSR       ; No, try next 
1501 0b74 7e 0d b8                       JMP         PHSR        ; Yes, fire phasors
1502 0b77 81 36              NPHSR       CMPA        #'6         ; Torpedo shot? ( was $B6 )
1503 0b79 26 c9                          BNE         CMD         ; No, illegal command, try again
1504 0b7b 7e 0d 32                       JMP         TRPD        ; Yes, shoot torpedo
1505                         
1506                         
1507                         ; The long range scan routine outputs the contents of the current 
1508                         ; quadrant and the eight quadrants which immediately surround it. 
1509                         ; The number of alien ships, space stations, and stars in each of these 
1510                         ; quadrants is displayed as described in the first chapter. A message 
1511                         ; is output first indicating the current quadrant location of the space ship.
1512                         ; The contents of the three quadrants in the row above the 
1513                         ; current quadrant are then output by calling the LRR subroutine. 
1514                         ; If this top row is outside the galaxy, the contents will be output as 
1515                         ; all zeros by use of the RWC routine. The row containing the current 
1516                         ; quadrant is then output, followed by the row below the current 
1517                         ; quadrant. If this bottom row is outside the galaxy, its contents will 
1518                         ; be displayed as all zeros. A dividing line of dashes is output between 
1519                         ; each row. At the completion, the routine returns to input a new 
1520                         ; command. The long range scan routine begins at the label LRSCN. 
1521                         
1522 0b7e ce 02 4d           LRSCN       LDX         #MSG15      ; Set pointer to long range message 
1523 0b81 bd 05 06                       JSR         MSG         ; Print long range scan 
1524 0b84 bd 07 02                       JSR         QUAD        ; Print quadrant location 
1525 0b87 8d 25                          BSR         LRSCN1      ; Print row of dashes 
1526 0b89 96 4c                          LDAA        CQLSS       ; Fetch current quadrant 
1527 0b8b 16                             TAB                     ; Save temporarily 
1528 0b8c c4 38                          ANDB        #$38        ; Current quadrant in row no. 1? 
1529 0b8e 27 21                          BEQ         RWC1        ; Yes, top row clear 
1530 0b90 80 08                          SUBA        #$08        ; Indicate row -1 
1531 0b92 bd 07 60                       JSR         LRR         ; Set up and print top row 
1532                         
1533 0b95 8d 17              LR1         BSR         LRSCN1      ; Print separating row 
1534 0b97 96 4c                          LDAA        CQLSS       ; Fetch current quadrant 
1535 0b99 bd 07 60                       JSR         LRR         ; Set up and print middle row 
1536 0b9c 8d 10                          BSR         LRSCN1      ; Print separating row 
1537 0b9e 96 4c                          LDAA        CQLSS       ; Fetch current quadrant 
1538 0ba0 81 38                          CMPA        #$38        ; Current quadrant in row no. 8? 
1539 0ba2 24 12                          BCC         RWC2        ; Yes, bottom row clear 
1540 0ba4 8b 08                          ADDA        #$08        ; No, set quadrant row +1 
1541 0ba6 bd 07 60                       JSR         LRR         ; Set and print bottom row 
1542 0ba9 8d 03              LR2         BSR         LRSCN1      ; Print bottom border 
1543 0bab 7e 0b 39                       JMP         CMND        ; Input next command 
1544 0bae 7e 07 27           LRSCN1      JMP         NTN         ; 
1545                         
1546 0bb1 8d 08              RWC1        BSR         RWC         ; Print clear row 
1547 0bb3 7e 0b 95                       JMP         LR1         ; Continue long range scan 
1548                         
1549 0bb6 8d 03              RWC2        BSR         RWC         ; Print clear row 
1550 0bb8 7e 0b a9                       JMP         LR2         ; Finish long range scan 
1551                         
1552 0bbb ce 04 c9           RWC         LDX         #Msg36a     ; Set pointer to left quadrant (was $04C9)
1553 0bbe 4f                             CLRA                    ; Set zero entry 
1554 0bbf bd 07 3c                       JSR         QDSET       ; Set quadrant contents 
1555 0bc2 ce 04 cf                       LDX         #Msg36b     ; Set pointer to middle quadrant (was $04CF)
1556 0bc5 4f                             CLRA                    ; Set zero entry 
1557 0bc6 bd 07 3c                       JSR         QDSET       ; Set quadrant contents 
1558 0bc9 ce 04 d5                       LDX         #Msg36c     ; Set pointer to right quadrant (was $04D5)
1559 0bcc 4f                             CLRA                    ; Set zero entry 
1560 0bcd bd 07 3c                       JSR         QDSET       ; Set quadrant contents 
1561 0bd0 7e 07 92                       JMP         LRP         ; Print long range row 
1562                         
1563                          
1564                         ; The galaxy display routine produces an output of the entire galaxy 
1565                         ; contents to the display device in a format similar to that of the long 
1566                         ; range scan. The display is used to provide the operator with a map 
1567                         ; from which a course may be charted for the mission. The contents of 
1568                         ; a complete row are set up in the galaxy printout message on page 00 
1569                         ; by calling the QDSET subroutine, and then the row is output to the 
1570                         ; display device. A dividing line of dashes is output between each row. 
1571                         ; When the output is finished, the routine returns to the command input
1572                         ; routine.
1573                         
1574 0bd3 ce 04 22           GXPRT       LDX         #MSG29      ; 
1575 0bd6 bd 05 06                       JSR         MSG         ; Print GALAXY DISPLAY
1576 0bd9 c6 31                          LDAB        #$31        ; Set number chars to print
1577 0bdb bd 07 29                       JSR         NT1         ; Print border 
1578 0bde ce 00 c0                       LDX         #GALSTART   ; Set pointer to galaxy ( was $00C0 )
1579 0be1 df 20                          STX         PNTR1       ; Store temporarily
