1853                         
1854                         ; The phasor routine fires a designated amount of phasor energy at 
1855                         ; the alien ships in the quadrant. The EIN subroutine is called to input 
1856                         ; the energy to be fired. The amount of energy entered is then deleted 
1857                         ; from the main storage bank. The number of alien ships in the immediate
1858                         ; quadrant is then determined to calculate the amount of 
1859                         ; energy to be fired at each. If there are no alien ships, a message is 
1860                         ; output indicating the energy fired was wasted. The amount of phasor 
1861                         ; energy to be fired at the alien ships is calculated and saved for use by 
1862                         ; the ASPH subroutine. 
1863                         ;
1864                         ; The ASPH subroutine is called to fire the phasor at each of the 
1865                         ; three possible alien ships in the quadrant. It first ascertains the 
1866                         ; presence of the particular alien ship by looking for its row and 
1867                         ; column location in the data table. If this location contains a CO, no 
1868                         ; alien ship is located here and the routine simply returns. Otherwise, 
1869                         ; this row and column location is output to inform the operator which 
1870                         ; alien ship is about to be attacked. The distance between the space 
1871                         ; ship and the alien ship, as defined in Chapter One, is then calculated 
1872                         ; and the distance factor is used to determine how much of the phasor 
1873                         ; energy actually reaches the alien ship. This energy is subtracted from 
1874                         ; the alien ship’s shield energy, and if the result is zero or less, the alien 
1875                         ; ship is destroyed. A message is output to inform the operator of its 
1876                         ; destruction. If the alien ship is not destroyed, the new energy level of 
1877                         ; the alien ship’s shields is output and, in retaliation, the alien ship 
1878                         ; fires a phasor equal to one quarter of its shield energy at the space 
1879                         ; ship. When the ASPH subroutine has completed its operation, it returns
1880                         ; to the phasor routine. After all alien ships in the quadrant have 
1881                         ; been fired upon, the phasor routine returns to the command input routine.
1882                         
1883 0db8 ce 04 33           PHSR        LDX         #MSG30      ; Print ‘PHASOR ENERGY TO FIRE=’
1884 0dbb 8d d2                          BSR         TR3         ; 
1885 0dbd bd 08 28                       JSR         EIN         ; Input energy amount
1886 0dc0 2b f6                          BMI         PHSR        ; Input error? Try again
1887 0dc2 bd 05 8a                       JSR         DCBN        ; Convert decimal to binary
1888 0dc5 de 28                          LDX         STORE2      ; Move binary energy value to proper
1889 0dc7 df 26                          STX         STORE1      ; Storage for ELOM routine
1890 0dc9 bd 08 1d                       JSR         ELOM        ; Delete energy from main supply
1891 0dcc bd 09 60                       JSR         WASTE       ; Check for presence of alien ships
1892 0dcf bd 05 11           PHS1        JSR         ROTR4       ; Position alien ship number 
1893 0dd2 80 01                          SUBA        #$01        ; 1 alien ship, full energy
1894 0dd4 27 04                          BEQ         PH1         ; 2 alien ships, half energy
1895 0dd6 16                             TAB                     ; 3 alien ships, Vt energy
1896 0dd7 bd 08 0f                       JSR         DVD         ; Divide energy accordingly
1897                         
